    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency trio of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.15), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.06), and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against King (4.37 xERA) and a favorable batting order position that elevates his run-production potential. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** (62.88) draw an ideal target in Ober (4.79 xERA). The decision to start **Miguel Vargas** over marginal options is validated by his xwOBA of 0.387 and a significant 19% SP Skill boost, which outweighs the inherent risks of facing a high-velocity arm. **Kyle Tucker** (66.99) remains a high-floor selection even against the lefty Alvarez, as his base projection provides enough padding to ignore the minor platoon regression.\n\nStrategic benching remains critical as we navigate our daily caps. **Wade Meckler** (36.92) serves as our most notable bench candidate, falling just short of the 40.0 threshold. While his platoon advantage is favorable, facing Skenes (3.26 xERA) presents a daunting SP Skill penalty that effectively erased the upside of his batting order spot. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Nasim Nunez**; while his projected 51.34 score is decent, we are banking on the 85% SB success rate against the opposing pitcher to justify his inclusion despite the #9 hole. Conversely, we must maintain caution with **Gunnar Henderson** (51.91); while he is a lineup lock, the 15% platoon penalty against Tolle represents a significant downward pressure on his expected output today. As we monitor the recovery of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, we remain cautious about pushing our depth players like **Wade Meckler** until the environment provides a more favorable path to stolen base opportunities.",
